                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da2318bb-af35-38ad-81b5-11648fe10497",
                        "entry_id": "648e572f-478f-3aaa-b3c7-f0e50295f0a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets vervelends"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "93bd9c78-3de8-4d95-85a8-ca7a1bfc8852",
                                "sense_id": "da2318bb-af35-38ad-81b5-11648fe10497",
                                "text": "Ook in de Nederlandse pers maakte de verschijning van Griet op de Beeck in ‘Zomergasten’ indruk. ‘Telkens gaf Griet lucht door te vertellen over de spirit waarmee mensen hun malheur te boven kunnen komen. En dat wondermooi verwoord in zangerig Vlaams. De ‘grondeloze eenzaamheid’ van haar jeugd, haar eetstoornis, haar doodswens op enig moment ... het mocht allemaal besproken worden’, schrijft columnist Han Lips in Het Parool."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cd52647-9b09-4e1a-96f6-e72a42c18c5b",
                                "sense_id": "da2318bb-af35-38ad-81b5-11648fe10497",
                                "text": "\"Iedereen zal wel een stuk of vijf uitvallers hebben. Maar acht, zoals ik? Ik betwijfel het?\", zegt Welten. En ondanks zoveel malheur scoort hij nog alleraardigst. In de Prominententour, de subleague waarin 16 bekende Tukkers het tegen elkaar opnemen, staat hij na etappe 11 van woensdag op plek 7, slechts 24 punten achter nummer 4: de Enschedese wethouder Eelco Eerenberg. \"Dat ik ondanks al die uitvallers in het linkerrijtje sta, daar ben ik best trots op. Helemaal omdat ik, in tegenstelling tot wat ik soms lees over anderen, mijn team helemaal alleen heb samengesteld. Mijn doel is om 'in Parijs' in de bovenste helft te eindigen.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e6998525-b27b-43f8-96ef-19e32801bef7",
                        "source_entry_id": "648e572f-478f-3aaa-b3c7-f0e50295f0a0",
                        "source_sense_id": "da2318bb-af35-38ad-81b5-11648fe10497",
                        "source_sense_description": "iets vervelends",
                        "target_lang_word": "misery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "misery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16020650-2d61-3e7f-b9f4-e85791bb44fc",
                                        "entry_id": "e3fc0a3a-a23a-3c66-8a67-473aaa6dbc9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Great unhappiness; extreme pain of body or mind; wretchedness; distress; woe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "843f3f29-76a1-4325-932a-e1f86ff408f1",
                                                "sense_id": "16020650-2d61-3e7f-b9f4-e85791bb44fc",
                                                "text": "Ever since his wife left him you can see the misery on his face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f0b8704-e49e-4238-a8c2-0a72e7a44b28",
                                                "sense_id": "16020650-2d61-3e7f-b9f4-e85791bb44fc",
                                                "text": "For miſerie doth braueſt mindes abate, / And make them ſeeke for that they wont to ſcorne, / Of fortune and of hope at once forlorne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26192730-f9fe-4d5b-ae46-83c72117a231",
                                                "sense_id": "16020650-2d61-3e7f-b9f4-e85791bb44fc",
                                                "text": "It was not just the confusion that unhappiness brings, it was not just the loneliness, it was the despair that accompanies all those emotions that turns unhappiness into utter misery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff8901d5-162c-47f5-abbf-dfaf3e00db22",
                                                "sense_id": "16020650-2d61-3e7f-b9f4-e85791bb44fc",
                                                "text": "Then, in January, a creeping tsunami of train cancellations, triggered by major staff absences as a result of the aggressive transmissibility of Omicron, heaped further misery on rail users."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e16716ed-2583-3e91-bc56-10329fdeaa1f",
                                        "entry_id": "e3fc0a3a-a23a-3c66-8a67-473aaa6dbc9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bodily ache or pain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ceb5ed3f-e497-45f7-a46d-714d5a630e82",
                                                "sense_id": "e16716ed-2583-3e91-bc56-10329fdeaa1f",
                                                "text": "[...] and I had a misery in my left breast and shoulder. I was hurt, but knew not how or how much."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7a59426-a495-304a-83fb-b9e9f7ef795d",
                                        "entry_id": "e3fc0a3a-a23a-3c66-8a67-473aaa6dbc9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cause of misery; calamity; misfortune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ac0ebb5-869d-3d1f-bb74-47c6da410d92",
                                        "entry_id": "e3fc0a3a-a23a-3c66-8a67-473aaa6dbc9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "poverty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cbb79ca-bef5-4de0-85be-b752972b913b",
                                                "sense_id": "4ac0ebb5-869d-3d1f-bb74-47c6da410d92",
                                                "text": "The Widdow that hath but a pan of braſſe, […]\nMuſt pay her Landlord many a groat,\nOr twil be puld out of her throat: […]\nThe rich haue all, the poore liue in miſerie: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
